{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1785530024313047002,"compiled_state":{"alias":"affable-soulless-gosling","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":6,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"4cfb5894e021b2128f7ef61c4a9a6d21d84b64f86361ffc8b2ff576a55081851","event_uuid":"705f61db-3c77-48b3-b88d-399bdad625df","position":{"commit_sha":"579cf4ad3bceccd72380319c876aaae302042541","position":"1785529749817352001-705f61db-3c77-48b3-b88d-399bdad625df"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"b232470fbe62bac9962f47c5c2cc1062f40b8edcf38e2068c9f74bc47bc63cd3","event_uuid":"a60189ba-112f-422b-a103-28a433712b0d","position":{"commit_sha":"fa3e31c5ccbc12a258cd3368f9279913a433d635","position":"1785529753241224001-a60189ba-112f-422b-a103-28a433712b0d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"76d62990a5b4f09c7ac366cff08c18f04c69c8583a8dd47c19f8ea7e752e4bc3","event_uuid":"dcd2e384-6047-4178-b233-4fe5ce2ef529","position":{"commit_sha":"e2ed4968b72402e23b1c98ccd58e4030b178d6c2","position":"1785530024313047001-dcd2e384-6047-4178-b233-4fe5ce2ef529"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"duplicate","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"INVESTIGATED BY THE OWNING SESSION, AS THIS TICKET ASKED. The observation was real and correctly\nreported; the candidate root cause it offered is WRONG, and the actual cause is now fixed and proven.\n\nThank you for filing it rather than investigating — the \"candidate, not a finding\" framing was exactly\nright, and the observation is what led here.\n\n=== THE OBSERVATION IS REAL. THE STATED CAUSE IS NOT. ===\n\nReported: \"DC inbound filing is a no-op ... no local ticket created from DC issue\". The actual defect\nwas in the TEST'S ASSERTION, not in inbound filing. Filed and fixed as\n[rebar:23ed-de0a-765b-49aa], merged as change 1124.\n\nThe assertion could never have passed, for two independent reasons:\n\n  * `_jira_key_to_local_id` LOWERCASES (`inbound_translate.py:120-124`): `RBJNAZV-1` becomes\n    `jira-rbjnazv-1`. The test's `remote_key in json.dumps(t)` check is case-sensitive.\n  * the inbound CREATE payload (`apply_inbound_records.py:183-212`) carries NO raw Jira key at all —\n    the key appears only as a TITLE FALLBACK, unused whenever the issue has a summary, as it does\n    here (\"J7 provenance oracle\").\n\nVerified against the exact payload shape the inbound path writes: `remote_key in json.dumps(ticket)`\nis False. So a PERFECTLY-CREATED ticket produced a red, and a genuinely-missing one would have too —\nthe oracle could not distinguish them in either direction.\n\nAlso worth correcting for the record: `filed=0` in that stdout is NOT the count of tickets filed from\nDC issues. `filed` counts INVARIANT-VIOLATION bug tickets (`run_differs.py:282`,\n`check_at_most_one_local_id`), so `filed=0` is healthy and says nothing about inbound. `scanned=1`\nand `OK: applied 1 of 1 mutations` were, in fact, consistent with a correct inbound create all along.\n\n=== PROOF THAT INBOUND FILING WORKS ===\n\nGitHub Actions run **30660546548**, job \"jira DC harness smoke\", against main @ fde6baae7 (the first\nmain containing the fixed oracle):\n\n    [jira-live-canary] collected=17 executed=17 skipped=0\n    1 failed, 16 passed in 13.55s\n\n`test_a_dc_created_ticket_carries_the_shared_jira_provenance` **PASSED**. It now asserts:\n  * a local ticket exists whose id EQUALS `_jira_key_to_local_id(remote_key)` — exact match on the\n    derived id, not a substring scan of a JSON blob;\n  * the BINDING STORE maps that local id to the DC key, so the ticket corresponds to THAT issue;\n  * `creation_channel == \"jira\"`.\n\n`executed=17 skipped=0` matters as much as the pass count: nothing silently skipped.\n\nThe single remaining failure in that run was\n`test_the_documented_setup_refuses_to_read_the_pat_from_config`, an unrelated credential defect filed\nas [rebar:cd78-d877-3d25-4ec3] and since merged.\n\n=== WHY THIS WAS NEWLY VISIBLE, WHICH THIS TICKET GOT RIGHT ===\n\nYour reasoning that bug 8070's fix un-masked the tier is correct, and it is worth recording that\nTHREE defects were masking this assertion in sequence, each hiding the next:\n  1. an EMPTY store made the pass report `scanned=0` and \"converged\" — indistinguishable from working;\n  2. the PAT-cap bug [rebar:f391-806b-938f-45d8] killed the suite at SETUP before the test ran;\n  3. the oracle itself could not pass (23ed).\nOnly with all three fixed does this test's verdict carry information.\n\nDISPOSITION: closing as a duplicate of [rebar:23ed-de0a-765b-49aa], which is the same underlying issue\ndiagnosed to its actual cause and already fixed, merged and closed. No inbound-filing defect exists.","timestamp":1785529749817352001}],"created_at":1785520786072205001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"dac88e7f-10c3-4692-82ac-c6fc90cf23f8","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"5f48-244c-7063-42d0"},{"link_uuid":"c08b753d-b06c-4abc-8319-20debca80919","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"8070-3f8b-8e71-483b"},{"link_uuid":"a60189ba-112f-422b-a103-28a433712b0d","relation":"duplicates","target_id":"23ed-de0a-765b-49aa"}],"description":"## Reported by, not investigated by, an adjacent session\n\nSurfaced while confirming the fix for bug 8070 (external-integration canary). Per operator\ninstruction this was NOT investigated — epic e369 is actively held by another session and owns this\nsubject matter. Filing it here so the owning session sees it. **The root cause below is a candidate,\nnot a finding.**\n\n## Observed (live CI, reproducible)\n\nRun 30651750699 — `workflow_dispatch` of `.github/workflows/external-integration.yml` on `main` at\ncommit `b7e6ac963`, 2026-07-31. Job **\"jira DC harness smoke (real Jira Data Center, ephemeral)\"**:\n\n```\ntests/external/live_jira_dc/test_reconcile_pass.py:319\nAssertionError: no local ticket was created from DC issue RBJNAZV-1;\n  stdout='invariants: scanned=1 filed=0 (cap=5)\\nOK: applied 1 of 1 mutations\\n'\nassert []\nFAILED test_reconcile_pass.py::test_a_dc_created_ticket_carries_the_shared_jira_provenance\n```\n\nThe failing test is `test_a_dc_created_ticket_carries_the_shared_jira_provenance`.\n\n## Why this is newly visible\n\nThis failure was previously MASKED. Until `b7e6ac963` the whole external tier died at\n`SnapshotRefError` on an unborn `HEAD` before reaching any behaviour under test (bug 8070). With\nsnapshot resolution fixed, the tier now reaches its subject and this assertion fails on its merits.\nSo this is very likely a pre-existing defect that the canary could not previously report, not a new\nregression from `b7e6ac963` — which touched only `tests/external/conftest.py` (adds an empty root\ncommit) and added a unit test.\n\n## Candidate cause — UNCONFIRMED, do not treat as diagnosed\n\n`scanned=1 filed=0` says the inbound record was seen and then not filed. That shape is consistent\nwith OPEN bug **5f48-244c-7063-42d0** — \"DC inbound identity mint fails silently: 'jira-datacenter'\nis not a valid creation_channel\" — where a silent mint failure would drop the record between scan\nand file. Linked `relates_to`. If that is the cause, this ticket is a duplicate and should be closed\nas such rather than worked separately.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The mechanism behind `scanned=1 filed=0` is identified and cited (`path:line`), and it is\n      determined whether this is the same defect as 5f48 (close as duplicate) or distinct.\n- [ ] `test_a_dc_created_ticket_carries_the_shared_jira_provenance` passes against the live DC\n      harness, or the failure is guarded by a credential-free test in the default suite.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["parent","e369-a449-4773-48fb"],["relates_to","5f48-244c-7063-42d0"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"e369-a449-4773-48fb","parent_status_uuid":"dcd2e384-6047-4178-b233-4fe5ce2ef529","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"0059-c7f0-cce1-4077","ticket_type":"bug","title":"DC inbound filing is a no-op in live CI: reconcile reports scanned=1 filed=0, no local ticket created from DC issue","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["d6dbfe9c-7194-4654-84bd-6a9bd5b96405","705f61db-3c77-48b3-b88d-399bdad625df","a60189ba-112f-422b-a103-28a433712b0d","dcd2e384-6047-4178-b233-4fe5ce2ef529"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785530024313047002,"uuid":"a8cc1a6e-54a9-47c4-8e59-2ee7b8e27477"}